# Local Development Environment Variables
# Copy this to .env.local and customize as needed

# =============================================================================
# Local R2 (MinIO) Configuration
# =============================================================================
# These settings allow using MinIO as a local S3-compatible storage
# instead of Cloudflare R2 for development and testing.

# Bucket name for materialized data storage
R2_BUCKET=warehouse

# Custom endpoint URL (enables local mode, skips Cloudflare account ID validation)
# MinIO default port from docker-compose.test-dbs.yml is 19000
R2_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:19000

# MinIO access credentials (default from docker-compose.test-dbs.yml)
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin

# =============================================================================
# Usage
# =============================================================================
# 1. Start MinIO using docker-compose:
#    docker-compose -f docker-compose.test-dbs.yml up -d minio minio-seed
#
# 2. Copy this file:
#    cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# 3. Run the application with local environment:
#    source .env.local && cargo run
#
# Or use dotenv to automatically load .env.local
